# --- Dedicated backend (provisioned, NOT yet usable) ---
# A separate Supabase project was created for this deployment via Mission
# Control's clone pipeline: ref `plisdzywzleljorrphxv`
# (https://plisdzywzleljorrphxv.supabase.co, org Xenochrome 3, ap-southeast-2).
# It is ACTIVE_HEALTHY but its schema is EMPTY — the migration replay could not
# reconstruct the prime's 546-table schema from the repo. Do NOT point the app
# here until a real schema clone lands; keep the prime values above. Full run
# log and every error: docs/BACKEND_PROVISIONING.md.
# VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="plisdzywzleljorrphxv"
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://plisdzywzleljorrphxv.supabase.co"

# --- Workspace identity & support ---
# VITE_AURIXA_BILLING_UID identifies this workspace to Aurixa Mission Control
# (entitlements, billing, and the support portal handoff). Defaults to
# "npc-prime" when unset — see src/hooks/useWorkspaceEntitlements.tsx and
# src/lib/missionControl.ts.
# VITE_AURIXA_BILLING_UID="npc-prime"

# Base URL of the Aurixa Systems Support Portal opened from the Support page.
# Trailing slashes are stripped; workspace/user identity is appended as query
# parameters. Defaults to https://www.aurixasystems.com.au/support when unset.
# VITE_SUPPORT_PORTAL_URL="https://www.aurixasystems.com.au/support"

# --- Client-facing deployment mode ---
# When "true", the build hides developer/operator tooling (Integrations
# credential cards, Workflow Playground, engine diagnostics, test-data
# controls) from navigation AND routing, and disables the pricing-mock
# toggle. Build-time only — no URL or localStorage override, by design.
# Visibility only, never access control; see docs/CLIENT_FACING_MODE.md
# and src/lib/clientFacing.ts. Defaults to off (the internal console).
# VITE_CLIENT_FACING="true"

# --- Server-side vendor secrets (Supabase Edge Function secrets, NEVER VITE_) ---
# Anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the browser bundle by Vite and is
# therefore public. Vendor keys belong in the Supabase project's function
# secrets instead:
#
#   supabase secrets set GOOGLE_FONTS_API_KEY=...
#
# GOOGLE_FONTS_API_KEY backs the `google-fonts-catalog` edge function, which is
# the only thing that may hold it. Template Builder's font picker previously
# called googleapis.com from the browser with this key written into
# src/hooks/useGoogleFonts.ts, so it shipped in every build. Without the secret
# set, the picker falls back to its curated list — degraded, not broken.

# --- MCP tooling (local dev only, NOT bundled into the app) ---
# API key for the @21st-dev/magic MCP server referenced in .mcp.json as ${MAGIC_API_KEY}.
# Generate one at https://21st.dev/magic/console, then copy this file to .env.local and
# fill in the value (or export MAGIC_API_KEY in your shell before starting Claude Code).
# Leave blank here — never commit a real key.
MAGIC_API_KEY=""

# API key for the hosted `21st` HTTP MCP server referenced in .mcp.json as
# ${TWENTY_FIRST_API_KEY}. Sent as the `x-api-key` request header. Generate one at
# https://21st.dev/magic/console, then copy this file to .env.local and fill in the
# value (or export TWENTY_FIRST_API_KEY in your shell before starting Claude Code).
# Leave blank here — never commit a real key.
TWENTY_FIRST_API_KEY=""
